From b0518e5af2a7b4553064f86200af541ee3de62f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "William Mark Katzenmeyer, P.E., C.F.M." <heccommander@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:16:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] hdf5-reader: cache old-style group names; add
 Group::member_names

[L05] Status vs upstream v0.9.3: NOT UPSTREAM.
Kind: performance + API. Proposed upstream grouping: PR-C performance/API.
Applies on roteiro-gis/netcdf-rust v0.9.3 (3d708fd) after the earlier patches of this series.

Listing or looking up children of a large old-format (symbol-table) group
re-read the local heap for every child name. Cache each group's names and
object-header addresses in the file context (keyed by group address, no
back-reference to the context), read the local heap data segment once per
first enumeration with checked offsets, terminators and UTF-8, and skip
the heap read for empty groups.

Add Group::member_names, which partitions child names into groups and
datasets without constructing Dataset objects or loading attributes.
Adds testdata/empty_heap_past_eof.h5; the cache regression test uses an
external fixture (HDF5_READER_CACHE_FIXTURE) and skips without it.
